# SS-05 - Native desktop pattern learning and replay
Workstream ID: SS-05
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/5
Status: DONE
Milestone: M1
Dependencies: SS-03, SS-04

## Purpose
Let users choose a stock/pattern, inspect real candles and learn causal simulated decisions.

## Tasks
- [x] Build PySide6 controls, background fetching, rule explanations and candle/fill charts.
- [x] Add equity/benchmark, replay cursor, visible fill ledger and full JSON export.
- [x] Invalidate stale results when parameters change and disclose unavailable features.
- [x] Exercise native rendering, replay, error states and export.
- [x] Record visual inspection separately from user acceptance.

## Acceptance criteria
- Network work does not run on the GUI thread; no future candles/fills/metrics leak in replay.
- Actual dataset identity remains visible even if request controls subsequently change.
- Export includes observations and assumptions; no broker or AI feature is falsely advertised.

## Completion evidence
- Desktop tests pass for replay, worker success/failure, closing during a fetch,
  parameter invalidation, dataset identity, export contents and insufficient history.
- Inspected a real-data 1600x1150 offscreen native render: readable controls,
  provenance, candle/fill and equity charts, explanation and fill ledger.
- Initial missing-glyph failure was traced to Windows offscreen font discovery;
  the script explicitly loads installed Segoe UI. Source links use a readable accent.
- Offscreen inspection does not qualify every normal Windows display/DPI configuration.
- Human acceptance remains pending independently of technical completion.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-11: Implemented native M1 interface; visual and runtime checks in progress.
- 2026-11-11: Completed automated native behavior checks and real-data visual inspection.
  Human acceptance and packaged Windows delivery remain separate SS-11 gates.
